Five Java sources in at/klausbetz/provider are vendored from tag
1.17.0, commit 665011f7ef021850ce5e7a92e33a8bf969c9a29f:
AppleIdentityProvider.java, AppleIdentityProviderConfig.java,
AppleIdentityProviderEndpoint.java, AppleUserRepresentation.java,
TokenExchangeParams.java.

Compatibility change in AppleIdentityProvider.java (marked in its header):
removed obsolete @Override annotation on exchangeExternalTokenV1Impl, since
Keycloak 26.8 replaced that SPI. AppleIdentityProviderEndpoint.java adds
@jakarta.ws.rs.ext.Provider for Quarkus REST subresource discovery and @Vetoed
to preserve broker-owned (not CDI-injected) request-specific construction; the upstream
empty META-INF/beans.xml is also retained. The other three files are unchanged. Both old
and current exchange methods are blocked by the Tessera wrapper.

The upstream factory and mappers are deliberately excluded. Only the Tessera
factory is registered. Tessera modifications live in a separate package.

